  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 6 files (2 deduped) that establish the dependency graph for this refactor:\n\n1. **`babel/package.json`** \u2014 root manifest of the source repo (v7.22.9); establishes what's changing.\n2. **`next.js/packages/next/package.json`** \u2014 the actual published `next` package's manifest. Lists `@babel/core`, `@babel/parser`, `@babel/traverse`, `@babel/generator`, `@babel/types`, `@babel/code-frame` and multiple `@babel/plugin-*`/`preset-*` packages under `devDependencies`, plus `webpack: 5.86.0` also under `devDependencies` \u2014 the edges to both other repos, though notably declared as dev, not production, dependencies (Next.js vendors/bundles these via ncc rather than resolving them from a consumer's node_modules).\n3. **`next.js/packages/next/src/bundles/babel/bundle.js`** \u2014 proves the devDependency listing is not decorative: this file directly `require()`s `@babel/core`, `@babel/parser`, `@babel/traverse`, `@babel/generator`, `@babel/types` at runtime, wiring Babel's parser into Next's own compiler bundle.\n4. **`next.js/packages/next/src/build/babel/loader/transform.ts`** and **`index.ts`** \u2014 the actual `next-babel-loader` implementation that invokes this bundled Babel to parse/transform user source \u2014 the concrete site where a new `DecoratorMetadata` AST node would surface.\n5. **`next.js/packages/next/src/build/webpack-config.ts`** \u2014 imports `webpack` from `next/dist/compiled/webpack/webpack`, establishing the Next.js \u2192 webpack edge (a vendored/compiled copy, version-pinned per the `webpack: 5.86.0` devDependency).\n6. **`next.js/package.json`** (monorepo root) \u2014 corroborates the same Babel/webpack devDependency pins at the workspace level.\n7. **`webpack/package.json`** \u2014 shows `@babel/core`, `@babel/preset-react`, and `babel-loader` appear ONLY under `devDependencies` (used for webpack's own test fixtures/build tooling), while webpack's actual `dependencies` for JS parsing are `acorn` + `acorn-import-assertions`, not Babel. This is the \"expected but not reached\" edge \u2014 webpack's production module-parsing pipeline does not consume Babel's AST at all.",
